# C11 statechart template tree (RFC §5.J.1, Phase A5)
#
# Foundation only — statechart emitter lands in M4+:
#   M2: forge/c/lookup.h.jinja2 + lookup.c.jinja2 (vertical slice in
#       sibling forge/ tree, exercises C11 emitter pipeline first)
#   M3: forge/c/{transform,condition,codec,validator}.{h,c}.jinja2
#   M4: c/state_machine.{h,c}.jinja2 — RTC + event queue + datamodel
#       in C11 with no `malloc`, `_Static_assert` invariants, fixed-size
#       arrays sourced from `<sce:capacity>` / deploy.yaml
#   M5: §5.O traceability (`#line` directives + sce_sourcemap.json)
#       integrated into all C11 templates
#
# Per RFC §5.J.1, generated C11 must:
#   - Use `<stdint.h>` integer types (uint8_t, uint16_t, ...)
#   - Use `_Static_assert` for compile-time invariants
#   - Avoid varargs in generated code
#   - Avoid `malloc` (heapless throughout)
#   - Share helpers via `sce_forge_runtime.h` (M3+)
#
# Mesh codegen for C11 is explicitly out of scope (the watching-zenoh
# downstream project does not consume Mesh codegen — see RFC §5.K).
